## SQLAlchemy conventions (2.0 style — enforce consistently)

- Use `select()` + `session.execute()` — **not** `db.query()` (legacy 1.x style).
- Use `Mapped[T]` type annotations with `mapped_column()` — not `Column()`.
- No `text()` raw SQL — use ORM constructs only.
- All DB access through `get_db` dependency injection — no module-level sessions.
- Services take `db: Session` as first arg; routers call services, never ORM directly.

```python
# Correct
from sqlalchemy import select
stmt = select(User).where(User.id == user_id)
user = db.execute(stmt).scalar_one_or_none()

# Wrong — do not use
user = db.query(User).filter(User.id == user_id).first()
```

## Session management

- `get_db` in `app/db/session.py` is the only way to obtain a session.
- Commit inside the service, not the router.
- Use `db.flush()` to get auto-generated IDs before the final commit when building related rows.
- Always `db.refresh(obj)` after commit if the response schema needs server-set fields (e.g., `created_at`).

## Model conventions

- Inherit from `Base` in `app/db/base_class.py`.
- Always include `created_at` and `updated_at` with `server_default=func.now()`.
- Use `DateTime(timezone=True)` for all timestamp columns.
- Use `cascade="all, delete-orphan"` on all parent→child relationships (see [`CONV-DELETE-CASCADE`](../../docs/CONVENTIONS.md#conv-delete-cascade) for the delete-endpoint contract: 204 + rely on cascade + cascade test).
- Filter every query by `user_id` — no cross-user data leakage (canonical: [`CONV-AUTH-OWNERSHIP`](../../docs/CONVENTIONS.md#conv-auth-ownership)).

## Data relationships

```
User → MealPlanWeek         (1:many, cascade delete)
User → Recipe               (1:many, cascade delete)
User → ChatSession          (1:many, cascade delete)

MealPlanWeek → PlannedMeal  (1:many, cascade delete)
MealPlanWeek → GroceryList  (1:many, cascade delete)

PlannedMeal ↔ Recipe via PlannedMealRecipe  (many:many; role = entree|side|etc.)
PlannedMeal  → PlannedMealRecipe  (1:many, cascade delete)
Recipe       → PlannedMealRecipe  (1:many, cascade delete)

Recipe → RecipeStep         (1:many, cascade delete)
Recipe → RecipeIngredient   (1:many, cascade delete; association to Ingredient)
Ingredient → RecipeIngredient (1:many; global catalog, append-mostly)
Ingredient → IngredientNutrition (1:1; catalog cache, not deleted with recipes)
Recipe → RecipeNutrition    (1:1, uselist=False, cascade delete)
Recipe → ChatSession        (1:many, cascade delete)

ChatSession → ChatMessage   (1:many, cascade delete)
GroceryList → GroceryItem   (1:many, cascade delete)
```

## Alembic

- Migrations live in `alembic/` only — no business logic there.
- Always import new models in `app/db/base.py` so Alembic autogenerate detects them.
- Generate migrations with: `uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "description"`
- Apply with: `uv run alembic upgrade head`
